1
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:06,620
Hello, Kentucky!
你好，肯塔基州！

2
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:15,790
Well, my fellow Kentuckians, thank you.
好吧，我的肯塔基同胞们，谢谢你们。

3
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:27,130
Tonight, I stand before you with gratitude and humility as the next United States Senator for the Commonwealth of Kentucky.
今晚，作为肯塔基州下一任美国参议员，我怀着感激和谦逊的心情站在你们面前。

4
00:00:30,481 --> 00:00:37,470
This election result is a victory for the people of Kentucky.
这次选举结果是肯塔基州人民的胜利。

5
00:00:38,470 --> 00:00:42,290
A victory for freedom over big government.
自由战胜大政府。

6
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:46,870
A victory for prosperity over dependency.
繁荣战胜依赖。

7
00:00:47,730 --> 00:00:51,150
A victory for safety over lawlessness.
安全战胜了无法无天。

8
00:00:51,610 --> 00:00:56,350
And a victory of common sense over socialism.
以及常识对社会主义的胜利。

9
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:08,860
I am grateful because this victory could not have happened without the sacrifice and hard work of so many.
我很感激，因为如果没有这么多人的牺牲和辛勤工作，就不可能取得这场胜利。

10
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:13,940
I first want to thank our divine creator who has endowed us with life,
我首先要感谢我们神圣的造物主赋予了我们生命，

11
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:16,200
Liberty, and the pursuit of happiness.
自由，追求幸福。

12
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:23,800
And blessed us with a country founded to secure those inalienable rights.
并祝福我们拥有一个为确保这些不可剥夺的权利而建立的国家。

13
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,400
I also want to thank my family.
我还要感谢我的家人。

14
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:31,000
You all mean the world to me, and I love each of you so much.
你们对我来说意味着整个世界，我非常爱你们每一个人。

15
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:37,020
To my beautiful wife, Davis, and my four precious children, Eleanor, Mary Clay,
致我美丽的妻子戴维斯和我的四个宝贝孩子埃莉诺、玛丽·克莱，

16
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:41,080
Hale, behind the podium, and Virginia.
讲台后面的黑尔和弗吉尼亚。

17
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:45,440
My most important job will always be as a husband and father.
我最重要的工作永远是作为丈夫和父亲。

18
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:49,520
But for the last 2 years, each of you has sacrificed so much,
但在过去的两年里，你们每个人都牺牲了很多，

19
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:52,960
Especially in time away from your husband and dad.
尤其是在远离丈夫和父亲的时候。

20
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:59,540
I simply could not have achieved this victory without your patience, forbearance, love, And support.
如果没有你们的耐心、忍耐、爱，我根本不可能取得这场胜利，并支持。

21
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:02,160
And that, I am truly grateful.
对此，我真的很感激。

22
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:16,760
To my mother and father, Garland and Donna Barr, thank you for instilling in me and my siblings the values of honesty,
感谢我的父母加兰和唐娜·巴尔，感谢你们向我和我的兄弟姐妹灌输诚实的价值观，

23
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:21,500
Hard work, persistence, faith in God, and compassion for others.
勤奋、坚持、对上帝的信仰和对他人的同情心。

24
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:28,260
To my entire extended family on the stage, and to those loved ones who are no longer with us,
对于舞台上的整个大家庭，以及那些不再和我们在一起的亲人，

25
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:36,680
But who remain in our hearts, I am so incredibly grateful for your love and all you have done to make this night possible.
但对于那些留在我们心中的人，我非常感谢你们的爱以及你们为让这个夜晚成为可能所做的一切。

26
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:47,016
Thank you to my supporters.
感谢我的支持者。

27
00:02:51,510 --> 00:02:59,090
To the volunteers, the door knockers, and the phone bankers, to the people who placed signs on their property,
对于志愿者、敲门者、电话银行工作人员、以及在他们的财产上放置标志的人们，

28
00:02:59,610 --> 00:03:02,390
And the friends who encouraged others to support our cause.
还有那些鼓励他人支持我们事业的朋友。

29
00:03:02,890 --> 00:03:10,015
Thank you to the good and hard-working people of Kentucky's 6th Congressional District,
感谢肯塔基州第六国会选区善良而勤奋的人民，

30
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:22,040
Who have given me the extraordinary privilege of representing them in the US House of Representatives for the last 14 years.
他们给了我非凡的荣幸，让我在过去 14 年里代表他们进入美国众议院。

31
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:31,960
It has been an honor of a lifetime, and together, we have accomplished much to make life better for the families,
这是一生的荣幸，我们一起取得了很多成就，让家人的生活变得更好，

32
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:34,940
Businesses, and communities of Central Kentucky.
肯塔基州中部的企业和社区。

33
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:41,380
Thank you to my staff, an amazing group of tireless, dedicated, and talented people.
感谢我的员工，他们是一群不知疲倦、敬业且才华横溢的优秀人才。

34
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:44,320
I couldn't have done it without you.
没有你我不可能做到这一点。

35
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:50,150
Thank you.
谢谢你。

36
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:57,410
And our hearts are especially with my late district director and campaign manager, Tatum Dale.
我们的心尤其与我已故的地区总监和竞选经理在一起，塔图姆·戴尔.

37
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:08,940
And last but not least, I want to thank my opponent Charles Booker.
最后但并非最不重要的一点是，我要感谢我的对手查尔斯·布克。

38
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:12,620
We disagree emphatically on many issues.
我们在许多问题上存在严重分歧。

39
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:14,680
But competition is good.
但竞争是好事。

40
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:21,220
It's a sign of a healthy democracy and I appreciate Mr. Booker's participation in it.
这是健康民主的标志，我感谢布克先生的参与。

41
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:33,990
I am reminded of the Gospel of Luke in which Jesus responds to a dispute which arose among his disciples as to which of
我想起了《路加福音》，其中耶稣回应了他的门徒中发生的关于哪一个是哪一个的争论。

42
00:04:33,990 --> 00:04:36,530
Them was considered to be the greatest.
他们被认为是最伟大的。

43
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:41,710
Jesus said to them, "The king of the Gentiles lord over them.
耶稣对他们说：“有外邦人的王作他们的主。

44
00:04:42,230 --> 00:04:47,050
Those who exercise authority over them call them themselves benefactors.
那些对他们行使权力的人称他们自己为恩人。

45
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:49,690
But you are not to be like that.
但你不应该那样。

46
00:04:50,370 --> 00:04:57,950
Instead, the greatest among you should be like the youngest and the one who rules like the one who serves.
相反，你们中最伟大的人应该像最年轻的人一样，统治者应该像服务者一样。

47
00:04:58,990 --> 00:05:10,370
So whether you voted me voted for me or not, my pledge is to assume this responsibility with humility and serve all Kentuckians regardless
因此，无论您是否投票给我，我的保证是谦虚地承担这一责任，并为所有肯塔基人服务

48
00:05:10,381 --> 00:05:12,390
Of political party or philosophy.
政党或哲学。

49
00:05:18,510 --> 00:05:24,250
So my friends, now that we have won, what comes next?
那么我的朋友们，既然我们赢了，那么接下来呢？

50
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:26,350
Let me tell you.
让我告诉你。

51
00:05:27,350 --> 00:05:30,284
I have a vision for Kentucky.
我对肯塔基州有一个愿景。

52
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:32,250
My vision is optimistic.
我的愿景是乐观的。

53
00:05:33,050 --> 00:05:37,630
It's a future defined by prosperity, opportunity, and growth.
这是一个由繁荣、机遇和增长定义的未来。

54
00:05:38,090 --> 00:05:47,810
From Pikeville to Paducah, from Covington to Corbin, and everywhere in between, it's time for Kentucky to become even stronger.
从派克维尔到帕迪尤卡，从卡温顿到科尔宾，以及其间的任何地方，肯塔基州是时候变得更加强大了。

55
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:58,460
It's time for paychecks to go up and prices to come down.
现在是工资上涨、物价下降的时候了。

56
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:05,900
It's time for more jobs, more opportunity, and more wealth for everyone, everywhere.
现在是为世界各地的每个人提供更多就业机会、更多机会和更多财富的时候了。

57
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:14,000
It's time for more freedom, limited government, less crime, fewer drugs, more coal,
是时候更多的自由、有限的政府、更少的犯罪、更少的毒品、更多的煤炭、

58
00:06:14,515 --> 00:06:22,940
More energy, more bourbon, faster horses, unwavering support for the most powerful military in the world.
更多的能量，更多的波本威士忌，更快的马匹，对世界上最强大的军队的坚定支持。

59
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:40,540
Now, ladies and gentlemen, socialism may be on the rise in some places in the United States,
现在，女士们先生们，社会主义可能在美国的一些地方正在兴起，

60
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:44,784
But not here in Kentucky.
但不是在肯塔基州。

61
00:06:50,130 --> 00:06:53,750
Not now, not tonight, not ever.
不是现在，不是今晚，也不是永远。

62
00:06:56,100 --> 00:07:03,980
To achieve our vision for America, to fight for freedom over socialism, it will take work.
为了实现我们对美国的愿景，为了争取自由而不是社会主义，我们需要付出努力。

63
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:08,380
But I promise you tonight, I will not shrink from it.
但今晚我向你保证，我不会退缩。

64
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:11,060
I will dedicate myself to it.
我将全身心投入其中。

65
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:18,820
And protecting our Constitution and our way of life is central to everything I will do.
保护我们的宪法和我们的生活方式是我所做的一切的核心。

66
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,760
I will protect and defend it.
我会保护和捍卫它。

67
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:27,900
I will guard against those who would expand the Supreme Court, weaken our military,
我将提防那些扩大最高法院、削弱我们军队的人，

68
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:36,245
Raise our taxes, and impeach our president.
提高我们的税收，弹劾我们的总统。

69
00:07:36,245 --> 00:07:41,250
Ladies and gentlemen, when I get to the Senate, I will roll up my sleeves and get to work.
女士们先生们，当我到达参议院时，我将卷起袖子开始工作。

70
00:07:41,970 --> 00:07:50,710
I will work with anyone from either party who loves the United States and is willing to make agreements that let us advance.
我将与两党中任何热爱美国并愿意达成让我们进步的协议的人合作。

71
00:07:51,710 --> 00:08:01,990
I am a proud Republican, but I will find those proud Democrats who are willing to work across the aisle to get good things
我是一名自豪的共和党人，但我会找到那些愿意跨党派努力以获得美好事物的自豪的民主党人

72
00:08:01,990 --> 00:08:03,130
Done for our country.
为我们的国家完成的。

73
00:08:10,175 --> 00:08:14,750
Up few of them still exist and I intend to find them.
其中很少有仍然存在，我打算找到它们。

74
00:08:18,190 --> 00:08:24,373
Before I close, I also want to thank my predecessor in this seat, Mitch McConnell.
在结束之前，我还要感谢在座的前任，米奇·麦康奈尔。

75
00:08:30,136 --> 00:08:37,900
He has served Kentucky with distinction and I wish Mitch and Elaine happiness and health.
他为肯塔基州做出了杰出贡献，我祝愿米奇和伊莱恩幸福健康。

76
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,740
They have both earned it.
他们都赚到了。

77
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:47,670
My friends, I love Kentucky like a lot.
我的朋友们，我非常喜欢肯塔基州。

78
00:08:54,180 --> 00:09:05,800
I am honored to hold office in this great state and I am grateful to you for electing me as your next United States Senator.
我很荣幸能够在这个伟大的州任职，我感谢你们选举我作为你们的下一任美国总统参议员。

79
00:09:09,250 --> 00:09:10,530
God bless you.
上帝保佑你。

80
00:09:11,830 --> 00:09:12,530
Thank you.
谢谢你。

81
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:22,230
God bless America's greatest Commonwealth and may God always bless the United States of America.
愿上帝保佑美国最伟大的本州，愿上帝永远保佑美利坚合众国。
